+## Find the gate actually used
+
+Follow a relevant caller through the selected client/decorator, limiter construction or registry
+lookup, acquisition and resource cleanup. Check runtime configuration and object lifetime, not only
+the class containing a semaphore. Record the paths and identities needed to establish coverage;
+include alternate launch paths that reach the same resource. A test of the wrapper alone does not
+establish that production callers use it.
+
+Two instances of `Semaphore(N)` each supply N permits. A gate created per request or per transient
+client cannot impose one shared N-operation limit. Use a stable gate for the protected scope, or
+account for the sum of intentional allocations. Repeated client construction is harmless to this
+bound if those clients really share the gate. Test concurrent requests through distinct entry
+objects: occupy the configured capacity, keep those operations open, and verify that an additional
+request is refused or waits according to policy.
